```

The error says "I already selected Enterprise to arrive at this point" - but the `keyType` selected on the page is different from their subscription tier. The user selected "Enterprise" as a key type on the page (which maps to `keyType: 'enterprise'`), but the server checks whether the user has a subscription tier of 'professional', 'enterprise', or 'custom'. The user likely doesn't have a subscription tier stored in the database yet.

However, since the error message literally says "Your current tier: none", this means the `userTier` is null. With my fix, if the user is logged in via Supabase and has a valid session, the auth header will be sent and the server can look up their tier. If no tier is set, the error will still appear, but now at least the API can correctly look up their tier.

But there's another problem: the user says they "already selected Enterprise to arrive at this point" - this implies they chose Enterprise on some pricing/subscription page, but that tier selection isn't being captured. The `/register/key` page doesn't receive subscription tier info.

